load ../termination-measure.maude

--- Coverage: a ring that advances once per round trip, carries the field
--- through on its other hop, is bounded somewhere, and consumes its token, is
--- admitted. This is the generator/critic ring.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-TERMINATION-MEASURE :
  hop(ra, 1) hop(rb, 0) bounds(ra) analysis(0, 0, false, true) =>! admitted .

--- Coverage: the one-rule ring is admitted on the same terms -- a loop spelled
--- in one rule is the loop of two rules with fewer names.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-TERMINATION-MEASURE :
  hop(ra, 1) bounds(ra) analysis(0, 0, false, true) =>! admitted .

--- Bite: nothing bounds the field, so the ring is never admitted however far it
--- advances. This is the nearest miss the diagnostic names.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-TERMINATION-MEASURE :
  hop(ra, 1) hop(rb, 1) analysis(0, 0, false, true) =>! admitted .

--- Bite: a ring that preserves its trigger is never admitted. Without the
--- consume there is no single token for a measure to speak about.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-TERMINATION-MEASURE :
  hop(ra, 1) bounds(ra) preserves(ra) analysis(0, 0, false, true) =>! admitted .

--- Bite: hops that only carry the field through are never admitted. The round
--- trip has to advance, not merely be readable.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-TERMINATION-MEASURE :
  hop(ra, 0) hop(rb, 0) bounds(ra) analysis(0, 0, false, true) =>! admitted .

--- Bite: hops that disagree in direction are never admitted, even bounded. A
--- field that can move back as easily as forward descends nowhere.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-TERMINATION-MEASURE :
  hop(ra, 1) hop(rb, -1) bounds(ra) analysis(0, 0, false, true) =>! admitted .

--- Bite: a walk that never returns to a value it has left never derives a
--- return, which is what admitting it rests on. This is the triage ring:
--- "queued" -> "routed", and the ticket is done.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-DOMAIN-MEASURE :
  walk(queued, routed) reaches(mtEdges) =>* returns RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Bite: a longer walk over the same finite domain still never returns, so the
--- closure is not an artefact of the two-value case.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-DOMAIN-MEASURE :
  walk(queued, routed) walk(routed, shipped) reaches(mtEdges) =>* returns RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Coverage: a walk that returns IS found, so the check has teeth. The domain
--- being finite is not the argument; not revisiting a value is.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-DOMAIN-MEASURE :
  walk(queued, routed) walk(routed, queued) reaches(mtEdges) =>* returns RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Coverage: an indirect return is a return.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-DOMAIN-MEASURE :
  walk(queued, routed) walk(routed, shipped) walk(shipped, queued) reaches(mtEdges)
  =>* returns RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Coverage: a bounded ring of releases is admitted. The item that comes round
--- is the item whose count advanced, which is what the guard reads.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-RELEASE-MEASURE :
  releases(ra) bounds(ra) analysis(0, false, true) =>! admitted .

--- Bite: nothing bounds the count, so the ring is never admitted. This is the
--- service loop the compiler warns about rather than refuses.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-RELEASE-MEASURE :
  releases(ra) analysis(0, false, true) =>! admitted .

--- Bite: a ring fed by `file` is never admitted however bounded its guard. The
--- guard reads a count on an item that a new item does not inherit.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-RELEASE-MEASURE :
  spawns(ra) bounds(ra) analysis(0, false, true) =>! admitted .

--- Bite: one spawning hop loses the ring even beside a releasing one. The
--- measure speaks about ONE item going round, and a ring that also mints items
--- is not that.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-RELEASE-MEASURE :
  releases(ra) spawns(rb) bounds(ra) analysis(0, false, true) =>! admitted .
